From 284939b2af603ac558a37b83b78ae2d580cbcdd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:23:54 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Provide arc4random() and its companions where the C library
 has none

glibc has had arc4random(), arc4random_uniform() and arc4random_buf()
only since 2.36 (2022), and Windows' C runtime has none of them.  Code
written for Apple's C library or a BSD's calls them freely, and on an
older glibc, such as Ubuntu 22.04's 2.35 (the oldest LTS still
supported, which AppImages are built on so they run on older systems),
it builds with an implicit declaration and then fails to link; on
Windows (MSYS2 CLANG64) it does not build at all.

Where they are missing the base library now declares them
(GSArc4Random.h, imported by NSObjCRuntime.h, so with Foundation),
exported from its DLL on Windows, and provides them in
Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c: bytes from getrandom(), or
/dev/urandom on a kernel without it, on glibc; from the C runtime's
rand_s() (the system's generator) on Windows; and arc4random_uniform()
without modulo bias.  On any other C library, glibc 2.36 and later
among them, the header declares nothing and the file compiles to
nothing.

The test calls the three functions through Foundation: on glibc 2.35 it
fails to link without this change and passes with it; on Windows it
fails to build without it and passes with it, and the Functions suite
passes.

Patch done with help of AI.
---
 Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h |   1 +
 Headers/GNUstepBase/GSArc4Random.h |  54 +++++++++++
 Source/Additions/GNUmakefile       |   1 +
 Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c    | 148 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 Source/GNUmakefile                 |   1 +
 Tests/base/Functions/arc4random.m  |  67 +++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 272 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Headers/GNUstepBase/GSArc4Random.h
 create mode 100644 Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c
 create mode 100644 Tests/base/Functions/arc4random.m

diff --git a/Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h b/Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h
index d30bb96..ddfa1fd 100644
--- a/Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h
+++ b/Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #import	<GNUstepBase/GSConfig.h>
 #import	<GNUstepBase/GNUstep.h>
 #import	<GNUstepBase/GSBlocks.h>
+#import	<GNUstepBase/GSArc4Random.h>
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <limits.h>
